{"name":"Lightning Bolt","hex":"#e5ebe6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lightning bolt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single, visible discharge of lightning.","A conventional representation of a lightning bolt as a zigzag line."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lightning_bolt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lightning","blocks":[{"text":"Lightning is a natural phenomenon consisting of electrostatic discharges occurring through the atmosphere between two electrically charged regions. One or both regions are within the atmosphere, with the second region sometimes occurring on the ground. Following the lightning, the regions become partially or wholly electrically neutralized."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/330px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning","wikidata":"Q33741"},{"title":"Thunderbolt","blocks":[{"text":"A thunderbolt, or lightning bolt, is a symbolic representation of lightning. It appears variously in history, literature, and in contemporary warnings of electricity. Thunderbolts may appear naturally among the estimated 8.6 million lightning strikes per day or not: heat lightning is an electrical discharge in the atmosphere without an accompanying sound, and a Tesla coil produces an artificial \"lightning\"-like electrical discharge with an accompanying clap. The term \"thunderbolt\" adds the notion of a loud thunderclap accompanying a lightning flash, while the term \"lightning bolt\" — which refers directly to the electrical discharge — does not."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/%D0%93%D0%9E%D0%A1%D0%A2_12.4.026-76_%E2%84%96_2.5.svg/330px-%D0%93%D0%9E%D0%A1%D0%A2_12.4.026-76_%E2%84%96_2.5.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunderbolt","wikidata":"Q2794866"},{"title":"Lightning Bolt (Pearl Jam album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lightning Bolt is the tenth studio album by the American rock band Pearl Jam. Produced by long-time Pearl Jam collaborator Brendan O'Brien, the album was released in the United States on October 15, 2013, through the band's own Monkeywrench Records, with Republic Records handling the international release one day earlier."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cd/Pearl_Jam_Lightning_Bolt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning_Bolt_(Pearl_Jam_album)","wikidata":"Q13780884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Earth_cutaway.png/500px-Earth_cutaway.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Earth_cutaway.png/500px-Earth_cutaway.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth_cutaway.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg/500px-Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg/500px-Anvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bolt from the blue lightning strike which appears to initiate from a clear patch of sky, but the turbulent sky above the anvil cloud drives a bolt of plasma through the cloud directly to the ground. They are commonly referred to as positive flashes, despite the fact that they are usually negative in polarity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnvil-to-ground_lightning.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF/330px-Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f4/Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF/330px-Ligtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALigtning_new_delhi_view_1.GIF"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Cloud_to_cloud_lightning_strike.jpg/330px-Cloud_to_cloud_lightning_strike.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Cloud_to_cloud_lightning_strike.jpg/960px-Cloud_to_cloud_lightning_strike.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Cloud_to_cloud_lightning_strike.jpg/330px-Cloud_to_cloud_lightning_strike.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACloud_to_cloud_lightning_strike.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Baltic_thunder.jpg/500px-Baltic_thunder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Baltic_thunder.jpg/960px-Baltic_thunder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Baltic_thunder.jpg/500px-Baltic_thunder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaltic_thunder.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/CC_lightning%2C_Albury_NSW.JPG/330px-CC_lightning%2C_Albury_NSW.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/CC_lightning%2C_Albury_NSW.JPG/960px-CC_lightning%2C_Albury_NSW.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/CC_lightning%2C_Albury_NSW.JPG/330px-CC_lightning%2C_Albury_NSW.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACC_lightning%2C_Albury_NSW.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Lightning_2012.jpg/330px-Lightning_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Lightning_2012.jpg/960px-Lightning_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Lightning_2012.jpg/330px-Lightning_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALightning_2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Understanding_Lightning_-_Figure_1_-_Cloud_Charging_Area.gif/330px-Understanding_Lightning_-_Figure_1_-_Cloud_Charging_Area.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Understanding_Lightning_-_Figure_1_-_Cloud_Charging_Area.gif/330px-Understanding_Lightning_-_Figure_1_-_Cloud_Charging_Area.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"(Figure 1) The main charging area in a thunderstorm occurs in the central part of the storm where the air is